# Vendored upstream source must stay byte-identical to what upstream
# published: ci/check_vendor_drift.py and tests/test_vendor_provenance.py
# both compare recorded SHA-256 hashes, and a checkout that rewrites LF
# to CRLF changes every one of them. That is what made the provenance
# test fail on Windows and only on Windows.
3rdparty/** -text
patches/** -text

# The corpus is fetched binary and hashed in the manifest.
.test_data/** -text
